I feel, how can I get approved
by my peers and classmates?

00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:56.400
I feel there is definitely
an impostor syndrome within me.

00:27:56.400 --> 00:28:01.880
So how did I get here, so
it took me some time to settle in.

00:28:01.880 --> 00:28:05.799
I felt overwhelming support
from all my classmates,

00:28:05.799 --> 00:28:10.250
whether they were internationals or
American classmates.

00:28:10.250 --> 00:28:14.940
And I feel, it just takes time,
so after the first quarter,

00:28:14.940 --> 00:28:19.631
after I found some rhythm and
retooled my life, it got better and

00:28:19.631 --> 00:28:24.620
better, now I feel like
I can be myself here.

00:28:24.620 --> 00:28:29.230
&gt;&gt; In my experience,
I would say that for me, the whole GSB

00:28:29.230 --> 00:28:34.660
experience to a large extent is a lesson
around the importance of focus.

00:28:34.660 --> 00:28:36.620
And that was especially tough and

00:28:36.620 --> 00:28:39.190
important during the first
couple of months at GSB.

00:28:39.190 --> 00:28:42.950
It's still an issue, but there are so
many things happening in parallel.

00:28:42.950 --> 00:28:46.982
You constantly need to prioritize,
there are so many questions to answer.

00:28:46.982 --> 00:28:51.151
What classes you prioritize, what type
of community within GSB should be your

00:28:51.151 --> 00:28:54.000
priority, how you approach
your career decision.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.210
There's so
many questions you need to answer,

00:28:56.210 --> 00:28:59.260
I think that was especially
difficult during the first quarter.

00:29:00.880 --> 00:29:05.054
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I think that as well,
I think coming from England,

00:29:05.054 --> 00:29:08.289
having not sat in a classroom for
a long time,

00:29:08.289 --> 00:29:12.738
when I started [INAUDIBLE] drinking
from a phial, [INAUDIBLE].

00:29:12.738 --> 00:29:17.707
And obviously with the court system here,
it is extremely dynamic.

00:29:17.707 --> 00:29:21.243
Ten weeks classes over ten weeks, so for

00:29:21.243 --> 00:29:25.490
me, it was really just getting
into the flow of things.

00:29:25.490 --> 00:29:28.880
And like you guys have touched on,
some balancing on the impostor syndrome,

00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:30.746
which I think everybody
has to some degree.

00:29:30.746 --> 00:29:35.170
How much to [INAUDIBLE] all of the other
activities that are running in parallel.

00:29:35.170 --> 00:29:38.890
And really coming to a realization
that you don't need to

00:29:38.890 --> 00:29:39.950
do every single one of them.

00:29:41.260 --> 00:29:46.212
So yeah, I think getting the balance
of the workload and your social life,

00:29:46.212 --> 00:29:50.472
and also taking some time to just
chill out and sing to yourself.

00:29:50.472 --> 00:29:55.446
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; So we're almost out of time today,

00:29:55.446 --> 00:30:00.144
but before I go, Argon and Hofsky,
any final words of advice for

00:30:00.144 --> 00:30:04.934
international students thinking
about applying to Stanford for

00:30:04.934 --> 00:30:07.370
MBA, maybe a couple words?

00:30:07.370 --> 00:30:11.689
&gt;&gt; Yeah, okay, sure, a couple words for
[INAUDIBLE], I would probably say that as

00:30:11.689 --> 00:30:17.000
all of us mentioned, it's to
a large extent about the community.

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:22.130
And I would suggest to spend some
time studying the community.

00:30:22.130 --> 00:30:26.220
Meet people from GSB who you can approach,
and just try to understand for

00:30:26.220 --> 00:30:29.708
yourself whether these are the people
you want to be around for

00:30:29.708 --> 00:30:31.534
the next two years of your life.

00:30:31.534 --> 00:30:38.677
And if the answer is yes [INAUDIBLE]
it's a fascinating place to be.

00:30:38.677 --> 00:30:43.279
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I think for me, it would just
be making sure that you have the best

00:30:43.279 --> 00:30:47.450
possible application for
yourself prepared before you apply.

00:30:47.450 --> 00:30:51.410
I think whether that's GMAT, whether
that's talking to current students,

00:30:51.410 --> 00:30:55.130
reaching out around your essays and
how to shape them, doing research for

00:30:55.130 --> 00:30:55.860
your essays.

00:30:55.860 --> 00:30:58.930
I think just make sure that you're
really putting your best foot

00:30:58.930 --> 00:31:00.480
forward before you apply.

00:31:00.480 --> 00:31:05.820
&gt;&gt; Yeah, as for me, my advice would
be just be yourself, be authentic.

00:31:05.820 --> 00:31:09.730
I think only you know what
you're truly passionate about.

00:31:09.730 --> 00:31:14.660
Only you know what kind of story you
can tell, you are unique as a person.

00:31:14.660 --> 00:31:18.130
So don't be afraid, be different,
having non-traditional

00:31:18.130 --> 00:31:22.090
background is not a problem, international
student, also, be proud of yourself.

00:31:23.480 --> 00:31:28.060
&gt;&gt; Okay, great, so now we'll wrap up,
thank you both for joining us, and

00:31:28.060 --> 00:31:31.230
thank you for everyone in the audience for
participating.

00:31:31.230 --> 00:31:33.548
You can learn more about
the MBA program and

00:31:33.548 --> 00:31:35.875
the admission process on the GSB website.

00:31:35.875 --> 00:31:40.830
The application for the next application
cycle will be available in June.

00:31:40.830 --> 00:31:42.650
Thanks again and have a great day.

